From 6a437082545c0da58c63bbbe5cff757be8085931
Subject: bevy_render: per-stage timings of the pipelined renderer as diagnostics
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/6a437082545c0da58c63bbbe5cff757be8085931
Date: 2026-09-22T23:04:15+01:00

Publish where a pipelined frame spends its time into the main world's
DiagnosticsStore, under `pipelined/`: the main update, the main world
waiting for the render app and blocked on the handoff, the render update,
and the render thread waiting for the handoff. On the web also the waits
for the GPU backlog and the next animation frame, and an estimate of GPU
time per frame from the fence buffers' map callbacks.

The render thread's figures are written to a static and read by the main
world at the next handoff, so the store is only touched from the main
world.

Opt in through `PipelinedRenderingDiagnosticsPlugin`, like bevy's other
diagnostics: it registers the paths and sets the flag the timing code
checks, so without it nothing is measured. The GPU and animation-frame
paths are only registered on the web, where they mean something.
---
